{"title":"2019 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Faster)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>Shonk sequence</i> is a sequence of positive integers in which\n</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: circle;\">\n<li>each term after the first is greater than the previous term, and</li>\n<li>the product of all terms is a perfect square.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For example: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee67283c870532df36c30af9a1f939be31b4e1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 6, 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> is a Shonk sequence since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d9211bff6cd63555f615900e9b1fefcd83f03328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f91e00ae6daeb0e897185b67ab794418e04755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27 &gt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa371e0e900504e502e131938cbaffc5a897bb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 6 \\times 27 = 324 = 18^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a94cc82589bf45ea163a9b24c38d7868fe264e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12, x, 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" /> is a Shonk sequence, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> but less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we can test every value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> (inclusive) until we get a perfect square because if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> doesn't work, we can infer that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> must be the value.\n</p><p>The product of all three numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9691772589e9ef72042e995174a05734658376d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\times x \\times 24 = 288x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/9141edf86d02f134b890bd556f2289d98aaf5608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d838fc4f474c1b350a580c1d13dc01705441693e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288 \\times 13 = 3744$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638797234a931f384fc3766f9c42bd87b0dff14f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^2 = 3600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7c5f10a0a57347cfa2988237d6583d9163885ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61^2 = 3721$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/d/b5d57aaeeae63e35d4bb4481e82bd3e4be2b71d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$62^2 = 3844$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />, so we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f0e0106bc114b97be479feb42dc8be507ea189b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3744$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> a perfect square.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/7559c5589729b2783559c301b88989b3b24e17a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56c1d2e89eb41a8c234c8806d8f0d25c8052094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288 \\times 14 = 4032$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca06bd9cb76eaecedf52735f54f6a72a43c62819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65^2 = 4225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782cd532ed6689ea4a9108c7469d21edc790c529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64^2 = 4096$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f2f307fc58e9a6098c72deacd3210675e5a88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63^2 = 3969$\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, so we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6395e1f759197dbcfc89b4990a2e34d913af689a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4032$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is <i>not</i> a perfect square.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a4662a1dcd96b0a6bc7d5abfe65f22109532a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9159001c18b0ad127c0dfc58c735e0c7f7b26f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288 \\times 15 = 4320$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca06bd9cb76eaecedf52735f54f6a72a43c62819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65^2 = 4225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/766beabc260a5e94b183cce7951846df2d6b47af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66^2 = 4356$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da22b8222c144f01ba03bf4a8f041ad88c2d381f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4320$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> a perfect square.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2cae13a8f6458d5d8c61ba965d0abb4b08da072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/7758b63158eaaf2d930a46a1f906f898d75965e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288 \\times 16 = 4608$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/766beabc260a5e94b183cce7951846df2d6b47af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66^2 = 4356$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c2942864c70ce085f1cf4ee21c933714add782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$67^2 = 4489$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/79345b404bc796316425b52ed833e3f74b64ee98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68^2 = 4624$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />, so we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/648222997ec8edb752bc4e0d5d17c90f7ea5190a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4608$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> a perfect square.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4e706959c6ef3bcaecc3e541404598c8cf3bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18accfc875c1cd494759f6ac79ecc2ff8aa27fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288 \\times 17 = 4896$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/4885b7e4f32905c01e2ba020f4e85f2206e4ccc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^2 = 4900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5b68ec821a093d953d9bc0679da7964eae719a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69^2 = 4791$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/358666d26bf38c132a89c4765411ef0cdb00ed63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4896$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> a perfect square.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d3e4315e912987aa3b30ed98d1a76b68101997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/898629aa63d73db174e10fee1418ae593abceb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288 \\times 18 = 5184$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. We find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/4885b7e4f32905c01e2ba020f4e85f2206e4ccc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^2 = 4900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc040368a40f452b8ccd35b2028839989dad2bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72^2 = 5184$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d3e78c0ffb6672e94b967763f7d419da9fdfb31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5184$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is a perfect square.\n</p><p>Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7ba21c54872f5ac820a1a3a06063b1fa1157d109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"66\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>We can also verify that later values don't work through similar trial and error.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Faster)\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6bed13bd63332ba2c289d4979841b4999763f747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\times 24 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 2 = (12^{2}) \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"270\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the square of some natural number for the product of all three numbers to be a perfect square.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d47c5390d91424f993e649434612ce0f47f8d6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 1^{2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />, which is too small because it is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/443c44432bb0867bd74c32b8e8b4b020996e0c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2^{2} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />, which is too small because it is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85762675850d14a6dfbd580d82a40a30d7750fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3^{2} = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />, which is large enough because it is more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7ba21c54872f5ac820a1a3a06063b1fa1157d109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"66\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>We also can verify that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/2/fd2e2d92f2ff802db3e1c9ac9d076acde7938cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 4^{2} = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> doesn't work, as it is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly, any natural number above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will result in an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> value more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so they do not work\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018011048\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 304/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 499/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11770/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.015      1 2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\n100.00%    7.015      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36929:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018011048 and revision id 285735. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}